{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR DECISION (2026-08-07): OPTION A — DROP inspect-ai.\n\ninspect-ai is never imported anywhere in src/ (zero `import inspect_ai` / `from inspect_ai` hits). The only reference is the `_optional.py` registry NAME, and `INSPECT_MIN_VERSION` is referenced by nothing. eval.py's docstring claims a routing that its own implementation comment explicitly disclaims ('NOT routed through Inspect AI... would add a dependency and an impedance mismatch for no gain').\n\nRemoving it dissolves three separate pieces of machinery that exist ONLY to accommodate it:\n1. BOTH `[tool.uv] conflicts` entries (`eval` vs `bedrock`, `eval` vs `dev`) — the diamond is [eval] -> inspect-ai -> aioboto3 -> aiobotocore pinning boto3 < 1.40.62 against pydantic-ai-slim[bedrock] needing boto3 >= 1.42.63.\n2. The `override-dependencies = [\"click>=8.3.3\"]` override — inspect-ai caps click < 8.2.2 for pallets/click#3084, which upstream fixed in click 8.3.2, so the cap is stale. That cap is what held the WHOLE project on vulnerable click 8.2.1 and made CI's gating pip-audit fail on every change in flight (PYSEC-2026-2132).\n3. This ticket's own problem: a smoke test gated on the [eval] extra would run in ZERO lanes, since only prompt-eval.yml's eval-live job installs it and that job is dispatch/weekly-only, continue-on-error, and pytest-less.\n\nAccepted cost: the published `[eval]` extra changes meaning for downstream consumers. That is a deliberate, documented break, not an oversight — it must appear in the CHANGELOG and release notes.\n\nExplicitly NOT chosen: (B) a mockllm canary lane would test upstream inspect-ai rather than any rebar code path — a dependency canary dressed as coverage. (C) building the inspect-ai path contradicts a decision already recorded in the implementation."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786114247092202001,"uuid":"183b445e-5d2f-4afb-bdda-c18cd1a84c66"}